course: dictionary
lesson: 15894
title: Unknowable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unknowable is built from three parts: un- (not), know, and -able (can be). Put them together and you get "cannot be known". «What the old king whispered in his last hour is unknowable now.» Nobody can find out, even with study or tools.
explain: Unknowable is not the same as unknown. If something is unknown, you do not know it yet, and you might find out later. If something is unknowable, it can never be found out. «The future is unknowable» means that no one can know for certain what will happen, however hard they study.
explain: Some things are unknowable because we cannot look inside them. «How my hamster truly feels inside is unknowable to me, though I can guess from how it moves.» Guessing is not knowing. When you read the clues around the word, you can see why the word fits.
fact: Unknowable means impossible to know or find out, even with study or tools.
fact: Un- means not, and -able means can be, so unknowable means cannot be known.
fact: Unknown means not known yet; unknowable means it can never be known.
fact: In science and philosophy, some things may be unknowable, such as what happened before the universe began.
fact: In a story, the word «unknowable» adds mystery, because the characters can never find out the truth.
exercise: «What the old king whispered in his last hour is unknowable now.» What does unknowable mean here? | Easy to guess from one small word | Very loud and clear | Written down in a book in the library | *Impossible to find out, even with study or tools
exercise: Ella says, «The future is unknowable.» What does she mean? | Tomorrow will be sunny for certain | Everybody knows what will happen next week | The future is a very long word | *Nobody can know what will happen, even with study or tools
exercise: Find and copy the word that means cannot be known: «The detective looked at the locked box, but its contents remained unknowable.» | detective | *unknowable | locked | box
test: «Whether the lost ship was ever found is unknowable.» Which word is closest in meaning to unknowable? | Funny | Fast | *Impossible to find out | Clear
test: Lily asks, «What does my dog dream about?» Why might the answer be unknowable? | The answer is written on the dog's collar | *Nobody can ask the dog or see its dreams, so it cannot be found out | Dogs never dream at all | Dogs can talk and tell us their dreams
exam: Which of these is best described as unknowable? | What 7 times 8 equals | *What someone else truly feels inside, even with careful study | Yesterday's weather | The colour of my bike
